{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","packSha":"9e187107ad1499186ae27b27b5e2e87e3db875902f21b89973b75a1db3fca7e6","packTokens":5290,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":67,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":678,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":939,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":3535,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":8,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Replace phone/email-based parts ordering with a self-service ordering portal\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Allow customers to quickly find parts using part numbers, product names, categories, and vehicle information\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Show each customer their applicable pricing and current stock availability\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Reduce manual order-entry work for office staff\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Give customers visibility into order status and invoices\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide staff with operational order queues and delivery information\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide management with basic sales and product reporting\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-8\",\n  \"text\": \"Maintain an auditable history of orders, invoices, customer accounts, and catalogue changes\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-9\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement customer authentication with sign-in, password reset, and account management\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-10\",\n  \"text\": \"Build product catalogue with search, filtering, categories, and vehicle compatibility\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-11\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement customer-specific pricing and price list management\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-12\",\n  \"text\": \"Manage stock availability with ERP CSV imports\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-13\",\n  \"text\": \"Build basket and checkout workflow with delivery date rules\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-14\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement order management with status tracking and staff editing capabilities\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-15\",\n  \"text\": \"Build customer order history, cancellation, and repeat order functionality\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-16\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement invoice creation, viewing, PDF download, and payment tracking\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-17\",\n  \"text\": \"Build administrative tools for product, user, category, and price list management\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Is the Customer Account Manager role in the first release? And can a Buyer see all of their company's orders (section 3.1) or only the orders they placed (section 3.2 implies only managers see other users' orders)?\",\n  \"answer\": \"No Account Manager role; every Buyer sees all of their company's orders and invoices\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Which invoices can a customer see? Invoices are only created when an order becomes Delivered (section 29), so should the invoice list simply show every invoice that exists for the customer's company?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Customers see every invoice that exists for their company; invoices only exist once the order is Delivered\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"After confirmation, which status changes can staff make? In particular, can staff cancel a Confirmed or later order for a customer who phones in?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Staff move orders forward one step at a time and can cancel any order that is not yet Delivered\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"What is recorded in the audit history for customer accounts and catalogue changes, and who can view it?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Who, when, and which fields changed (old and new values); admins only\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"Can customers create or edit their own delivery addresses, or are addresses maintained only by staff or admins?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Customers can only select from addresses that staff or admins maintain\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Customer Buyers can see all of their company's orders. Should saved basket templates also be shared with every Buyer in the company, or stay private to the Buyer who made them?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Templates are private to the Buyer who created them\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"There is no management role. Who can see the sales and product reports, and which reports are in the first release?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Office staff and admins; sales by period, sales by customer, and top products\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"How is stock checked when an order is placed or confirmed? Stock only changes with the nightly ERP import, and the portal never decrements it.\",\n  \"answer\": \"Compare the ordered quantity with the last imported quantity, without subtracting orders placed since the import\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall authenticate users by email and password, starting a session that carries the user's role and, for Customer Buyers, their company.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall allow signed-in users to sign out, invalidating their session.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall lock an account for 15 minutes after 5 consecutive failed sign-in attempts, rejecting sign-ins with a lock message during that time.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let users request a password reset by email, sending a single-use link valid for 1 hour to set a new password.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let administrators invite Customer Buyers or Office Staff via an emailed link valid for 7 days, through which the invitee sets a password and becomes active.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall block sign-in and order submission for deactivated users or users of inactive companies, while preserving their existing orders, invoices and history.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let administrators list users, deactivate/reactivate them, change their roles, or change a Buyer's company, showing role, company and status, applying changes on the user's next request, and keeping history.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall restrict each Customer Buyer to their own company's orders, invoices, prices, delivery addresses and account details.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall return a 403 error and make no change when a user calls a function reserved for Office Staff or Administrators without the required role.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let Customer Buyers search the catalogue by text term across name, code, part number or brand, case-insensitively.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let Customer Buyers filter catalogue results by a flat category, combinable with text or vehicle search.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let Customer Buyers search by vehicle attributes, returning products with matching compatibility records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall show product list and detail with required fields, including price, stock status, and additional description and compatibility on detail pages.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall show prices excluding tax from the price list assigned to the Buyer's company.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall show 'Price on request' and block basket addition for products missing a price or whose price list is deactivated.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall derive stock status from last imported quantity using configured thresholds.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall run a scheduled import job that updates stock quantities from a valid ERP CSV and logs applied/skipped counts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall preserve existing stock quantities and log a failure if the ERP file is missing, unreadable or invalid.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall maintain one persistent basket per Customer Buyer until order submission or emptying.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall validate basket quantity changes as whole numbers of 1 or more and compute line and subtotal totals.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall calculate the earliest delivery date based on cutoff time, working days and non-working dates.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall reject delivery dates that are non-working, too early, or beyond the booking horizon, naming the broken rule.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall offer only active delivery addresses belonging to the Buyer's company at checkout.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 24,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall reject order submissions where ordered quantities exceed last imported stock, without altering stock.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 25,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall reject order submissions when reviewed prices differ from current prices or items become 'Price on request'.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 26,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall create a new order with sequential number, Received status, and order details once checkout validation passes, then empty the basket.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 27,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall keep prices of existing orders and invoices unchanged when price lists are updated.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 28,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall allow Office Staff to progress order status only through the defined sequence or cancellation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 29,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall record a timeline entry for every order status change, including timestamp and actor.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 30,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall validate stock and company status when confirming a Received order, updating status or rejecting with reason.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 31,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall email the order recipient a confirmation detailing lines, prices, total and any staff-made changes upon confirmation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 32,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall require a reason when staff cancel or reject a non-Delivered order, updating status and emailing the recipient.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 33,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let staff amend quantities, lines, address, date and note on Received orders, recording amendment history.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 34,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall email the recipient when staff change or remove lines on a Received order.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 35,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall email the recipient when an order's status changes to Out for delivery.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 36,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let Office Staff create orders on behalf of customers, applying the same checkout rules and recording the staff creator.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 37,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let Office Staff view and filter the order queue by customer, date range and status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 38,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let Office Staff export a CSV delivery list of non-cancelled orders due on a given date.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 39,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let Office Staff export a CSV delivery list of orders due on a date, limited to in-progress or delivered statuses.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 40,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall show Office Staff and Administrators a dashboard with order counts, invoice status counts, and latest import result.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 41,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let Customer Buyers list their company's orders, filterable by status and date range.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 42,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let Customer Buyers view full order details including timeline, lines, totals, note and amendments.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 43,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let Customer Buyers cancel their own Received orders and reject cancellation attempts on other statuses.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 44,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let Customer Buyers repeat a previous order, adding available items to the basket at current prices and flagging unavailable ones.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 45,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let Customer Buyers save and reuse private basket templates with current pricing and availability flags.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 46,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall automatically generate an Unpaid invoice when an order becomes Delivered.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 47,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall compute invoice status as Paid, Overdue or Unpaid based on payment and overdue settings.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 48,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let Customer Buyers view their company's invoices and Office Staff/Administrators view all invoices with summary fields.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 49,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let authorized Buyers and Office Staff download invoice PDFs with required details.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 50,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let Office Staff mark invoices as paid with a payment date, recording the user.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 51,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let administrators manage product records, keeping retired products out of the catalogue but visible on orders/invoices.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 52,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let administrators manage single-level product categories and apply changes to catalogue filtering.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 53,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let administrators upload product images with file type and size restrictions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 54,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let administrators manage vehicle compatibility records per product.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 55,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let administrators manage price lists and their assignment to companies, maintaining one price per product per list.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 56,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let administrators create and edit customer companies with required details and status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 57,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let Office Staff and administrators maintain customer company details.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 58,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let Office Staff and administrators manage customer delivery addresses.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 59,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let Office Staff search customers and view their details, price list, orders and invoices.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 60,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let administrators edit and validate system settings, applying them to subsequent calculations.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 61,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall record an audit entry for every create, change or delete action on key entities.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 62,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall restrict audit history access to administrators and prevent editing or deleting entries.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 63,\n  \"text\": \"The portal shall let Office Staff and administrators generate sales reports by period, customer and top products, viewable on screen and exportable as CSV.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}